Fragments
description: a selected region, stored as a selector under the node's `yo: fragments:` key
- >
  *The implementation stores fragments as specified here; tagging still writes the legacy
  `yamlover-annotations` arrays until the membership rework lands.*
- >
  A **fragment** is a selected region inside a supported node: a text span, an image/PDF/djvu
  rectangle, a map box. A fragment holds **only what locates/highlights the region** - no
  description, no color, nothing else.
- >
  Simply selecting a region in the viewer **creates a fragment in the node the selection was
  made in**.
- >
  A fragment is ordinary data under the node's **`yo: fragments:`** key. Since yamlover reaches
  inside everything it holds - binary files included - fragments can be defined on any node.
- 'Defining fragments on a text chunk:'
- !!yo
  'reads the file twice: once to scan, once to build'
  yo: fragments:
    - once to scan
      type: text
      prefix: 'reads the file twice: '
      suffix: ', once to build'
    mykey: once to build
      type: text
      prefix: 'once to scan, '
      suffix: ''
- >
  `yo: fragments:` is a `kseq` - it holds keyed and keyless members alike. Each member is an
  **omni**: its **self-value carries the fragment's principal content** (for a text fragment,
  the selected text itself), the rest of the selector is spelled as fields beside it, and
  further fields may ride along. Each supported target has its own selector shape - one
  subchapter per type, below. The example above defines one keyless fragment and one named
  `mykey`.
- >
  Autogenerated member keys are **slugs** (`${base36(now)}-${rand}` - the scheme that used to
  name annotation files):
- 'The same chunk with viewer-created, slug-keyed fragments:'
- !!yo
  'reads the file twice: once to scan, once to build'
  yo: fragments:
    mqdo07z1-owgrcv: once to scan
      type: text
      prefix: 'reads the file twice: '
      suffix: ', once to build'
    mqdo0b44-k2n9pz: once to build
      type: text
      prefix: 'once to scan, '
      suffix: ''
- >
  When one fragment needs several names - or a place under an arbitrary path - yamlover's `&`
  bookmarks apply ([bookmarks](*::language:pointers:bookmarks)), spelled canonically on their
  own lines after the value:
- 'The `mykey` fragment, also reachable as `synonym` and pushed under an arbitrary path:'
- !!yo
  'reads the file twice: once to scan, once to build'
  yo: fragments:
    mykey: once to build
      &synonym
      &: put: me: also: here
      type: text
      prefix: 'once to scan, '
      suffix: ''
- *: text
- *: image
- *: pdf
- *: djvu
- *: map
- *: crop
- *: url
- *: future
